# Force LF in the repository and on checkout, regardless of a contributor's
# local core.autocrlf. Without this, a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true silently rewrites every text file's line endings to
# CRLF on checkout -- harmless for most files, but fatal for anything with a
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebang: `env` looks for a command literally named
# `bash\r`, which does not exist, and the container build dies with exit 127
# ("bash\r: No such file or directory"). Found while verifying native TLS
# support against a real cluster: `docker buildx build` of deploy/Dockerfile.local
# failed at `scripts/build-web.sh` for exactly this reason, on a checkout
# where every affected file's REPOSITORY content was already plain LF --
# only the working-tree copy autocrlf produced was CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
